    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d772">

                <pb facs="0734" n="618" sameAs="frus:frus1912/pg618"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 815.51/338.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                            Vice President of the Whitney Central Trust and Savings
                            Bank of New Orleans</hi>.</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1912-06-18">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">June 18, 1912</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: The Department has received your telegram
                    of the 8th instant, and your letter of the 11th of the same month, in regard to
                        <pb facs="0735" n="619" xml:id="pg619"/> the proposed temporary loan of
                    $500,000 to Honduras, and begs to say in reply that it has already taken up the
                    matter to which you referred with Mr. Zemurray, who has doubtless already
                    advised you of the substance of the interview.</p>
                <p>I am [etc.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">P. C. Knox.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
